+# Assistant UI, grounded fallback and gated server integration
+
+16 November 2026. Continues the approved Phase 10 specification/plan; no scope reapproval. Input is the latest tested Phase 10B bundle, Library `libfile_3c5f13bb22a081919caa289a4e02ecab`, SHA-256 `5e3080b357de0d8bd9a266410847a5e59d2fed711cb2df9a06be138033917755`. Preserve Help and account_sessions.py.
+
+## Product order and gates
+
+Deliver a usable in-app `/assistant` page now. Guests, native/local previews and unconfigured deployments use deterministic FAQ answers with real citations, sample questions, accessible form conversation and no external calls. This is a fallback, explicitly not model-generated prose. The AI entry point explains the distinction and illustrative data. Existing Help remains accessible if the assistant page is disabled.
+
+LLM requests still require verified account authority, explicit consent to sending the question, distinct opt-in to one selected authorized trip, and a ready provider/privacy/free-only/storage contract. No public fake login or unsigned identity adapter. No change to guest ownership or offline collections. Because verified sign-in, production PostgreSQL account/claiming and provider choice are unfinished, the public model path remains disabled. No private trip is passed to a provider by the current application.
+
+## Slices and actual source seams
+
+1. UI/fallback: tests against actual `app.create_app` for GET/POST, samples, no-JavaScript operation, CSRF, input escaping/bounds, no question in URLs/cookies, no-store responses, switch, catalog/draft/storage independence and native staging. Before implementation record meaningful 404/missing-navigation failures. `assistant_answers.py` maps questions to approved FAQ entries (versioned `help_content.py`); it does not guess arbitrary facts. `assistant_web.py` blueprint renders `templates/assistant.html`. Use existing theme tokens; no browser control/builds/emulators. Client enhancement is optional; server-rendered turn works alone.
+2. Server pipeline: executable tests first using actual account session service and Flask routes, with synthetic identities issued internally by pytest (never an HTTP login), a read-only synthetic account-owned trip gateway and deterministic fake provider. Test session/consent/selection gates, revalidation before dispatch and after response, sanitized single-trip context, citation whitelist and excerpt-only rendering, bounded context/output and all fallback conditions. A missing module is only an absence probe; use minimal API scaffolding if needed and validate real failing operations before behavior implementation. No fake database is labelled PostgreSQL evidence.
+3. Durable admission: separate explicit-create SQLite development quota adapter; never a production fallback or a write to existing trip databases. Transactionally enforce 5/minute and 20/UTC-day per account, 100/UTC-day globally, one in-flight/account and two globally across store objects/restarts. Count attempted calls on error. Invalid/unavailable quota storage denies model calls. Keep active reservations until actual task completion; no automatic expiry that could admit >2 still-running provider calls. Crash-abandoned reservations fail closed pending confirmed-worker-termination maintenance; local FAQs continue. Production activation requires a reviewed shared PostgreSQL adapter, still not available. Test real SQLite, fake time and bounded contention without stress tests.
+4. Optional HTTP adapter: server-only immutable allowlisted HTTPS endpoint/model/credential, no redirects/arbitrary URL fetching/tools; OpenAI-compatible chat JSON wire format is an adapter contract, not selection of a vendor. Model must select approved source IDs only; display server-owned exact excerpts and validated links, never arbitrary generated facts. Supply actual model token counter before configuration, total input <=6,000, output request <=600 tokens, body cap, end-to-end request deadline <=15s and no retry. Tests inject transport or a local-in-cloud fixture; no API calls/credentials. Check official current technical references before using wire-format claims. This does not establish any provider's free tier or legal suitability.
+
+## Context and answer contract
+
+Sources have server-defined ID, label, text, version and safe internal or approved catalog link. FAQ IDs resolve to `/help#...`; catalog IDs resolve to a new read-only `/assistant/sources/<id>` page which renders bundled attributed data, including illustrative currency/cost. No arbitrary client/model URL. Prefer FAQ sources without catalog access; catalog failure leaves FAQ fallback working. Citation existence alone is insufficient: model output is restricted to a bounded JSON source-ID selection, with answers rendered as exact source excerpts. Unknown IDs or extra fabricated text are rejected. Instructions in questions/catalog are untrusted and cannot gain tools or authority.
+
+Trip context is opt-in per request (stricter than remembering session consent), exactly one selected ID from the trusted account-trip gateway. Recheck authorization before every dispatch and before returning output; expiry/revocation/deletion/ownership loss discards late results. With no selection send no trip, even if the user browsed a trip page. Gateway is read-only and not an anonymous-save adapter. No guest row claiming is implied. Project only destination, allowed preferences, itinerary venue/slot/illustrative estimate fields; no trip title, email, account/row IDs, cookies, tokens or arbitrary free text. Reject overlarge context; do not truncate away rules. Production gateway remains absent until real account ownership/claiming is implemented and tested.
+
+Each request is a single conversation turn. No application transcript, browser local/session storage or transcript in signed cookies. Optional JS displays up to four turns in DOM only, clears on navigation/clear and sends no history to the provider. Zero prior turns is within the four-turn ceiling. Current source has no real logout endpoint; no-store plus clearing DOM on pagehide and authority revalidation are defense in depth, not proof of browser Back-cache behavior.
+
+## Verification and honest delivery
+
+Run the 77 existing account tests plus Help before/with final regressions. Keep red/green logs and exact counts. Add actual script tests only if JS is introduced. No change to current downloads or presentation materials; source staging resources can be added so a future build is complete. No live deployment, real database migration, secret rotation or external-account action. Keep accounts and live models disabled. Report browser/accessibility/native/real-PostgreSQL/live-model checks as pending when unrun. Identify specific provider/account/terms/configuration decisions needed; never ask for secret values in chat. This increment is not completion of verified sign-in, claiming, deletion or live AI.
